<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu Abdallah al-Shi'i</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/911">911 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu Abdallah al-Shi'i was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismailism">Ismaili</a> missionary who converted and organised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kutama-berbers">Kutama Berbers</a> of what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a> in the late ninth century. Leading them in war, he overthrew the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aghlabid-dynasty">Aghlabid dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifriqiya">Ifriqiya</a>. His campaign prepared the way for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdallah-al-mahdi-billah">Abdallah al-Mahdi Billah</a> to be proclaimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a>, making him a key figure in the foundation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a>.</p></div>
